===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|appurtenaunce}}, from {{der|en|xno|apurtenance}} and {{der|en|fro|apartenance}}, from {{m|fro|apartenir}}, from {{der|en|la|appertineō||I belong, I appertain}}.  Equivalent to {{suffix|en|appertain|ance}}. More at {{l|en|appertain}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Northern California, US}} {{audio|en|En-us-ncalif-appurtenance.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[appendage]] to something else; an [[addition]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1891|author={{w|Thomas Hardy}}|title={{w|Tess of the d'Urbervilles}}|publisher=James R. Osgood, McIlvaine and Co.|location=London|volume=1|page=36|passage=The youngsters, not immediately within sight, seemed rather bright and desirable '''appurtenances''' than otherwise; the incidents of daily life were not without humorousness and jollity in their aspect there.}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} [[equipment|Equipment]] used for some specific [[task]]; [[gear]].
# The thing to which another [[pertain]]s.
# {{lb|en|legal}} Minor [[property]], such as an [[outhouse]], that passes with the main property when it is [[sold]].
# {{lb|en|grammar}} A [[modifier]] that is [[append]]ed or [[prepend]]ed to another word to [[coin]] a new word that expresses belonging.

